	(text "J3 is an unresolved load interface.\nConfirm transducer/driver, current and protection.\nNo direct-drive suitability is assumed."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 175 162 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bd67c9ee-5518-5916-b933-2caada413c12")
	)
	(text "Wire colours are the breadboard jumpers in the owner photos\n(2026-09-24), not a harness specification.\nInland 1.3\" OLED V2.0 (KS0056), 4-wire SPI, 3.3 V.\nSH1106 128x64 inferred from the vendor example.\nJ2 pins follow the board header, pin 1 = GND (top).\nGPIO21 (A14, the e-ink BUSY) is unused."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 175 96.52 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d63a8518-71ff-50ff-851f-2e6c1f5a5c25")
	)
	(text "blue wire"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 204.47 79.76 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ed72d4f5-e5d8-5670-b024-bc1879904e5b")
	)
	(text "SCHEMATIC REVIEW / RELEASE HOLDS\n1. U1 uses A1-A19 / J1-J19 from SigilBackMarked.png (BACK view); never exchange row identities.\n2. No DevKit footprint assigned: measure pitch, row spacing, outline, USB-C overhang, holes, socket height and keepouts.\n3. Future footprint: two 1x19 female sockets, unmistakable A1/J1 marks; verify insertion from carrier component side.\n4. Keep USB-C, BOOT and EN/reset accessible; preserve antenna/component clearances after measurement.\n5. Display/joystick headers have no footprint and the buzzer is a logical interface; all are excluded from PCB and BOM.\n6. Buttons and LEDs are removed while the controls are redesigned; their GPIOs are NC here.\n7. Rev A is an electrical draft, NOT fabrication-ready. Power through DevKit USB; no second supply designed."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 28 211 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f9944de7-34f8-5c30-8e62-0242486d1968")
	)
